# libcss: background-size percentages read as auto
# Generated 2026-09-24 (Hermes fill-in, patch 84)
#
# MacSurf's background-size parser (fixes191b, see patch 59) accepted
# `auto` and px lengths only; a CSS_TOKEN_PERCENTAGE fell into the
# final else and returned CSS_INVALID, so `background-size: 100%`
# (and any percent form) was dropped and the property read as auto
# (gap in docs/phase-0/11). Each axis is now stored as -percent
# (clamped 1..100) in the same int16 slot: negative keeps its own
# tag next to the cover/contain sentinels instead of colliding with
# the explicit-px values 1..32767. The consumer side (patch 84,
# netsurf) resolves the percent against the positioning area.
# See docs/phase-0/11-real-sites.md.
diff --git a/src/parse/properties/p_background_size.c b/src/parse/properties/p_background_size.c
